+### Annotated Fields
+
+Field configuration, such as a custom name, description or deprecation reason,
+can also be added to a field by embedding a `strawberry.field` instance inside
+an [typing.Annotated](https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Annotated)
+type hint:
+
+```python
+from typing import Annotated
+import strawberry
+
+
+@strawberry.type
+class Query:
+    name: Annotated[str, strawberry.field(description="The name of the user")]
+    age: Annotated[int, strawberry.field(name="yearsOld")]
+```
+
+This is equivalent to assigning a `strawberry.field` to the attribute, but keeps
+the field definition in the type annotation. Any default value set on the
+attribute is used when the `strawberry.field` does not define one.
+
+<Note>
+
+Only one `strawberry.field` may be used per `Annotated` annotation. Using more
+than one raises a `MultipleStrawberryFieldsError`.
+
+</Note>
+
